WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.803
The headline finding is about robustness to
dimensionality.

00:00:03.883 --> 00:00:07.686
In every setting, the proposed test keeps the
type-one error at the nominal level,

00:00:07.766 --> 00:00:11.569
and crucially it still pinpoints the true change
point even when the state has ten,

00:00:11.649 --> 00:00:15.452
twenty, or thirty dimensions.

00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:19.335
By contrast,

00:00:19.415 --> 00:00:23.218
the CUSUM-RL baseline only recovers the change
point when the state is one-dimensional,

00:00:23.298 --> 00:00:27.101
and the ODCP method fails to control the type-one
error at all in high dimensions.

00:00:27.181 --> 00:00:30.984
The toy example confirms the double robustness in
action: size and power hold as long

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:34.867
as at least one of the two nuisance models is right,

00:00:34.947 --> 00:00:38.750
with the strongest power when both are correct.
